    "notes": "Recording dates: November 15, 1959; November 20, 1959; March 10, 1960 (Wikipedia and Plosin sessionography agree; MilesDavis.com gives the broader period Nov 1959 – Mar 1960). The November 15 session was devoted to an alternate take of Concierto de Aranjuez part 1; the November 20 session recorded the master/edited version of Concierto de Aranjuez (with José Mangual on percussion); the March 10 session recorded the remaining four tracks (with Elden 'Buster' Bailey on percussion and a slightly different brass section: Johnny Coles replaces Taft Jordan on trumpet, Bill Barber replaces Jimmy McAllister on tuba, and Joe Singer/Tony Miranda replace John Barrows/Earl Chapin on French horn). Jimmy McAllister appears on the November sessions (tuba), Bill Barber on the March session. John Barrows and Earl Chapin appear only on the November sessions; Joe Singer and Tony Miranda only on the March session. Taft Jordan only on the November sessions; Johnny Coles only on the March session. José Mangual Sr. only on the November sessions; Elden 'Buster' Bailey only on the March session. The AllMusic credits page is incomplete (it lists many personnel but does not include session dates or track-level assignments). Minor name variants resolved: Al Block/Albert Block; James/Jimmy Buffington; Bill/Billy Barber; José Manguel/Jose Mangual/José Mangual Sr. Track durations from Wikipedia and AllMusic are essentially the same. Cover art URL from Cover Art Archive for the MusicBrainz release associated with this release group."
  },
  "ballot": {
    "album": "Miles Davis — Sketches of Spain (1960)",
